'''''Briza minor''''' is a species of [[Poaceae|grass]] known by the common names '''lesser quaking-grass'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |access-date=2014-10-17 }}</ref> or '''little quakinggrass'''. It is native to the [[Mediterranean Basin]], and it is known elsewhere, including much of North America, as an [[introduced species]]. It is an annual grass producing narrow clumps of erect stems up to 50 centimeters tall. The [[inflorescence]] bears several small cone-shaped spikelets, each hanging on a [[Pedicel (botany)|pedicel]].

